> 
> Where voi'i : poi'i :: voi : poi

Actually, although that's a possible analysis, it's not quite
what I had in mind.

{voi} = {poi/noi ju'anai}
{voi'i} = {poi'i ju'anai}

(where {ju'anai} scopes over the following bridi). 

{le'i broda} = {le(i) du voi ke'a klesi lo'i broda}

IOW, voi gives pure nonveridicality, while le gives both
nonveridicality and specificity.

your {ce'u voi'i ke'a broda} = {ce'u poi'i ke'a du da voi broda}
-- it gives only nonveridicality, without the specificity.
Perhaps if you change your version to:
brode le'ei broda = kairbroda le du poi ke'a du'u ce'u voi'i ke'a broda
it would restore the requisite specificity.

